                              "content": "Breadth counts how many stocks are in long-term uptrends, not just whether the index is up. Narrow rallies (index up, breadth flat) have historically been more fragile. This series is slow — it moves over weeks, not days — which is why the chart matters more than today's number.  Learn more ›",
